<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $600 mln in Dec 16 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $600 mln in Dec 16 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $600 million in the December 16 week to $3,822.6 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $9.9 billion to $4,892.5 billion. M-1 rose $2.2 billion to $1,072.7 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,812.5 billion versus $3,806.1 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
